# Genkit Google AI Plugin API Key
# You can get an API key from Google AI Studio: https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# This key is used by Genkit to authenticate with the Gemini API.
# Rename this file to .env and add your API key.

# Option 1: Using GOOGLE_API_KEY
# GOOGLE_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY_HERE

# Option 2: Using GEMINI_API_KEY
# GEMINI_API_KEY=YOUR_API_KEY_HERE

# Choose one of the above and uncomment it, replacing YOUR_API_KEY_HERE with your actual key.

# Note: If deploying to some environments (like Firebase Functions with Secret Manager),
# you might configure the API key through environment-specific mechanisms instead of a .env file.
# Ensure that the .env file is listed in your .gitignore file to prevent committing your API key.
